{
  "description": "Meter readings, language-neutral: for a state from initialState({ value, min, max, low, high, optimum }) in core/src/meter/state.ts, percentage(state) is the filled share (0 to 100, compared to within 1e-9), level(state) the band of the value and quality(state) how good it is given where the good end sits. min defaults to 0, max to 100, optimum to max; low and high are unset when absent. The core tests and the Flutter tests read this file, so both implementations answer the same cases.",
  "readings": [
